l time. Profile neighbor-list/model overhead (try compile_model=True, larger skin). Use more atoms (>=2000) for finite-size control. Cu validation must land within about 50 K of 1357.77 K before the Al number is trusted.\"}}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/work/runs/report.json --parent $C | head -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":59962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":477,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5db0997-fcee-484a-a2e3-59451bf1f904","uuid":"40ce25e8-d553-4e88-9651-ecae6f47a81f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T10:05:36.203Z","request_id":"req_011Cgc27zQaRLZK5WeY3JpiF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0145zwhpTaYaMWsuzMkqZsDq":{"command":"cd /work; pkill -f coex.py; C=$(./board post candidate '{\"name\":\"aluminum\",\"family\":\"metal\",\"tier\":\"trust\",\"formula\":\"Al\",\"structure_source\":\"fcc Al, ase.build.bulk\",\"rationale\":\"Requested: melting point of Al at ambient pressure\"}' --fulfills 379402c9-d7b5-4fdc-a733-24b559d0ab28:0 | grep -o -E \"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f-]{27}\" | head -1); echo $C\ncat > /work/runs/report.json <<'EOF'\n{\"status\":\"failed\",\"task\":\"melting_point of Al at ambient pressure (two-phase coexistence, ALCHEMI NPT + MACE-MPA-0, Cu validation)\",\n\"reason\":\"Premise check passed: Tm of fcc Al at ~0 GPa is well defined and computable via solid-liquid two-phase coexistence (NPT, anisotropic, P=0), which avoids the superheating of single-phase heating. Planned validation: same setup on Cu vs ITS-90 fixed point 1357.77 K from /data/calibration/tier1.json. The run failed for lack of compute/agent budget. ALCHEMI NPT/NVT with MACE-MPA-0 (cuEq, float32, no compile) ran at about 1 s/step on the GB10 even for 2x640-atom boxes. The 8-system coexistence stage (Al 750-1050 K, Cu 1100-1550 K, 2000 steps) would have taken several hours, and the agent budget ran out first. Only solid NPT equilibration (Al a~4.13 A at ~900 K, solid stable) and part of the melt step finished. No coexistence data, no validation, so no melting point is reported. The experimental value (933.45 K, NIST-JANAF) was NOT reproduced by simulation and is not posted as a result.\",\n\"run_dir\":\"/work/runs\",\"attempt\":1,\n\"details\":{\"scripts\":\"/work/scripts/coex.py, common.py\",\"log\":\"/work/runs/coex.log\",\"engine\":\"ALCHEMI nvalchemi-toolkit 0.2.0\",\"model\":\"MACE-MPA-0 medium\",\"n_atoms_per_box\":640,\"timestep_fs\":2.0,\n\"next_steps\":\"Rerun coex.py with more wall time. Profile neighbor-list/model overhead (try compile_model=True, larger skin). Use more atoms (>=2000) for finite-size control. Cu validation must land within about 50 K of 1357.77 K before the Al number is trusted.\"}}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/work/runs/report.json --parent $C | head -3"}}}
